<===> README.md
In the indented syntax, `@else` belongs to an `@if` with the same
indentation, also if the `@if` is nested (libsass assumed indentation 0, so
a nested `@else` was an error and a less indented one was accepted).
<===>
================================================================================
<===> nested/input.sass
.a
  @if false
    b: c
  @else
    d: e
<===> nested/output.css
.a {
  d: e;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> nested_else_if/input.sass
.a
  @if false
    b: c
  @else if true
    d: e
  @else
    f: g
<===> nested_else_if/output.css
.a {
  d: e;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> deeper/input.sass
$x: 2
.a
  .b
    @if $x == 1
      c: d
    @else if $x == 2
      e: f
    @else
      g: h
<===> deeper/output.css
.a .b {
  e: f;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> root/input.sass
@if false
  a
    b: c
@else
  a
    d: e
<===> root/output.css
a {
  d: e;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> mixin/input.sass
@mixin m($v)
  @if $v
    a: yes
  @else
    a: no
.x
  +m(false)
.y
  +m(true)
<===> mixin/output.css
.x {
  a: no;
}

.y {
  a: yes;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> each/input.sass
.a
  @each $i in 1 2
    @if $i == 1
      one: $i
    @else
      other: $i
<===> each/output.css
.a {
  one: 1;
  other: 2;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> else_less_indented/input.sass
.a
  @if false
    b: c
@else
  d: e
<===> else_less_indented/error
Error: This at-rule is not allowed here.
  ,
4 | @else
  | ^^^^^
  '
  input.sass 4:1  root stylesheet
